IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 3: subsection (a), the exclusion.
-- Reading taken (fork F1 in NOTES.md): subsection (a) has TWO requirements, each aggregating 2 years in the 5-year period:
-- the ownership requirement (the property was owned) and the use requirement (it was used as the taxpayer's principal residence).
-- They need not be met at the same time. Subsections (b)(2)(A)(i)-(ii) and (d)(4)(A)-(B) speak of them separately.
-- "Principal residence" is not defined by the section: whether a stretch of time was use as the principal residence is a fact the caller states.
-- "2 years" is counted as the days in the 2 calendar years ending on the date of the sale or exchange (fork F6).

§ `Subsection (a): exclusion`

-- src:13 | (a) Exclusion
-- src:14 | Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a), the 5-year period (src:13-14)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A Span
`s 121(a) the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange` MEANS
    `the span of the years ending on` sale 5

-- src:14 | Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a), 2 years (src:14)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(a) 2 years, counted in days, ending on the date of the sale or exchange` MEANS
    `the days in the years ending on` sale 2

-- "has been owned ... by the taxpayer ... for periods aggregating 2 years or more": the ownership requirement.
-- `days included under (g)` is the aggregate that subsection (g) adds (0 where (g) adds none).
-- src:14 | Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a), the ownership requirement (src:14)
GIVEN `periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
      window IS A Span
      sale IS A DATE
      `days included under subsection (g)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` MEANS
    IF `the days of the spans inside the window` `periods of ownership` window PLUS `days included under subsection (g)`
         AT LEAST `s 121(a) 2 years, counted in days, ending on the date of the sale or exchange` sale
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer's principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more." (failed "if"; marginal reading (a) in NOTES.md)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- "... used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer's principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more": the use requirement.
-- src:14 | Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a), the use requirement (src:14)
GIVEN `periods of use as the principal residence` IS A LIST OF Span
      window IS A Span
      sale IS A DATE
      `days included under subsection (g)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) the use requirement is met` MEANS
    IF `the days of the spans inside the window` `periods of use as the principal residence` window PLUS `days included under subsection (g)`
         AT LEAST `s 121(a) 2 years, counted in days, ending on the date of the sale or exchange` sale
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer's principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more" (failed "if"; marginal reading (a) in NOTES.md)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Both requirements: "owned and used".
-- src:14 | Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a), the ownership and use requirements (src:14)
GIVEN holding IS A Holding
      window IS A Span
      sale IS A DATE
      `days included under subsection (g)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) the ownership and use requirements are met` MEANS
    `both are true`
        (`s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` (holding's `periods of ownership`) window sale `days included under subsection (g)`)
        (`s 121(a) the use requirement is met` (holding's `periods of use as the principal residence`) window sale `days included under subsection (g)`)

-- The operative sentence: gross income shall not include the gain, if the requirements are met.
-- This answers subsection (a) alone; subsections (b) to (g) limit or displace it, and are combined in s121-whole.l4.
-- src:13 | (a) Exclusion
-- src:14 | Gross income shall not include gain from the sale or exchange of property if, during the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange, such property has been owned and used by the taxpayer as the taxpayer’s principal residence for periods aggregating 2 years or more.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(a) (src:13-14)
GIVEN holding IS A Holding
      window IS A Span
      sale IS A DATE
      `days included under subsection (g)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(a) gross income does not include the gain` MEANS
    `s 121(a) the ownership and use requirements are met` holding window sale `days included under subsection (g)`
